  short="Most people feel well after their gallbladder is removed. Some continue to have pain, indigestion or loose motions. Causes include a stone left behind in the bile duct, a bile leak soon after surgery, bile-related loose motions, or a separate problem such as acidity or IBS. Tests find the cause, and most are treatable.",
